'''training-bit''' (trā′ning-bit), ''n.'' A wooden gag-bit used in training vicious horses. It has iron cheeks with a connecting iron passed through a wooden mouthpiece. ''E. H. Knight.''

'''training-day''' (trā′ning-dā), ''n.'' A day appointed by law for drill and review of the militia or other citizen soldiery.

